<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs-Monday actual 115,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs-Monday actual 115,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Actual interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog marketings Monday were 115,000 head, compared with the estimate of 110,000, according to USDA.</p>
<p>Early sales of barrows and gilts were steady to firm compared to midsession Monday.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    53.00 -54.00	   54.00 -55.00</p>
<p>liberal volume	 53.50- 54.00	   54.50 -55.00</p>
<p>few			52.50  54.50	   53.50  55.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to firm.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  43.50 -44.00	   42.50 -45.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   45.00 -50.00	   45.00 -50.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    50.00 -55.00	   50.00 -56.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
